// Occurrence-counting via `count where`. Permit reading only on the
// user's first 3 read requests within the last hour (rate limit by
// occurrence). The count is over distinct *tps* at which a Read by
// the current user has fired — repeated reads of the same document
// count separately. Compare to case 131, which uses `count d where
// Read(...,document: d)` and counts distinct *documents*; that gives
// the same answer here only because the trace uses 4 distinct
// documents.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
